      "question": "How is a drawing program parsed and run?",
      "status": "answered-statically",
      "authority": "direct-shipped-source-inspection",
      "answer": "This is JavaScript producing plain marks, not a separate declarative DSL. A lexical heuristic finds statement boundaries while skipping quoted strings/comments and tracking bracket depth; a cached scanner revisits only the last boundary on append. Top-level const/let are rewritten to var for persistent streamed scope. Session uses a generator with direct eval; runCode uses Function with(api). Syntax/runtime fallback retains earlier marks and reports errors. No shipped code was executed in this analysis.",
