      "question": "How is the hand-drawn look constructed?",
      "status": "answered-statically",
      "authority": "direct-shipped-source-inspection",
      "answer": "Deterministic seeded noise, densification, Catmull-Rom curves, bowed hand segments and perturbed ellipse samples produce centerlines. Tapered or even-width round-capped outlines become filled SVG paths. A white pathLength1 dash mask reveals strokes over time. Fill filters and glow metadata are separate. Fonts default to Patrick Hand, UI labels use system-ui, and card-mode text can use Barlow.",
