      "question": "How are labels and overlapping containers placed?",
      "status": "answered-statically",
      "authority": "direct-shipped-source-inspection",
      "answer": "Pieces try nearby label positions, reject overlap with prior pills/marks, and score remaining candidates by host busyFor plus distance/order cost. Layout approximates shape/text bounds, samples intersections on a14x14 grid and nudges colliding labelled containers by bounded candidate offsets; unresolved overlaps become warnings. Painter measured text/shape bounds provide a second placement pass. It is heuristic layout, not a proof of no overlap.",
