      "question": "What do ring, frame, paper and button concretely do?",
      "status": "answered-statically",
      "authority": "direct-shipped-source-inspection",
      "answer": "Ring expands a target box by4 screen points, chooses pill/small-round/bounded rounded-box radius and emits a bowed even-width line plus a collision-placed label. Frame emits tint/dashed outline with optional native marquee metadata. Paper emits a native window mark when hostDrawsWindows is true, else SVG sheet/chrome marks, then heading/subtitle and returns content bounds. Button emits a role/button dot with JSON action and optional fallback gel drawing.",
